  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2018-11-27T04:51:17.923Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "When an object sync object moves, all non owners will see the object's position interpolated from the original location to the new location. This works for general pickups to make them appear smooth for nonowners. If the goal is to instead teleport the object to another location, the object only teleports for the owner and jitters its way to the location for everyone else. This jitter not only looks bad, it takes time and can ruin logic. If there is a collider to detect this object, it is possible for it to be triggered by other players but not the owner since it interpolated itself through the collider.\n\nThe video in this tweet shows how the movement of the object sync'ed object looks to both the owner and everyone else.\nhttps://twitter.com/CyanLaser/status/1065855912131227648\n\nWhile one solution is to teleport the object for everyone locally, this is not possible in all cases as the teleport location may only exist on one player's game.",
